Messiah”, the official title of our Lord, occurring five hundred and fourteen times in the New Testament.","verses":1831,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Mary","v":[3,5,6,7,8,11,16,17,18,19,20,29,30]},{"id":"isaiah_617","name":"Isaiah","also":"Esaias","summary":"The son of Amoz (Isa. 1:1; 2:1), who was apparently a man of humble rank. His wife was called “the prophetess” (8:3), either because she was endowed with the prophetic gift, like Deborah (Judg. 4:4) and Huldah (2 Kings 22:14-20), or simply because she was the wife of “the prophet” (Isa. 38:1).","verses":53,"father":"Amoz","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"jesse_903","name":"Jesse","also":"","summary":"Firm, or a gift, a son of Obed, the son of Boaz and Ruth (Ruth 4:17, 22; Matt. 1:5, 6; Luke 3:32). He was the father of eight sons, the youngest of whom was David (1 Sam. 17:12).","verses":44,"father":"Obed","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"holy_spirit_7400","name":"Holy Spirit","also":"Comforter, Holy Ghost","summary":"The third Person of the adorable Trinity.","verses":246,"father":"","mother":"","v":[13,16,19,30]}],"places":[{"id":"illyricum_595","name":"Illyricum","kind":"Region","lat":43.51548,"lon":16.07154,"summary":"A country to the north-west of Macedonia, on the eastern shores of the Adriatic, now almost wholly comprehended in Dalmatia, a name formerly given to the southern part of Illyricum (2 Tim. 4:10).","verses":1,"v":[19]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[19,25,26,31]},{"id":"spain_1111","name":"Spain","kind":"Region","lat":40.48139,"lon":-3.17533,"summary":"Paul expresses his intention (Rom. 15:24, 28) to visit Spain.","verses":2,"v":[24,28]},{"id":"achaia_16","name":"Achaia","kind":"Region","lat":37.5,"lon":22.5,"summary":"The name originally of a narrow strip of territory in Greece, on the north-west of the Peloponnesus. Subsequently it was applied by the Romans to the whole Peloponnesus, now called the Morea, and the south of Greece.","verses":10,"v":[26]},{"id":"macedonia_747","name":"Macedonia","kind":"Region","lat":40.73292,"lon":22.9352,"summary":"In New Testament times, was a Roman province lying north of Greece. It was governed by a propraetor with the title of proconsul. Paul was summoned by the vision of the “man of Macedonia” to preach the gospel there (Acts 16:9).","verses":21,"v":[26]},{"id":"judea_657","name":"Judea","kind":"Region","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"After the Captivity this name was applied to the whole of the country west of the Jordan (Hag. 1:1, 14; 2:2).","verses":44,"v":[31]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["Barnes","JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[1473,3588,3588,1415,3784,941,941,941,3588,771,3588,3588,102,2532,3361,700,700,1438],[1538,1473,1473,700,700,3588,4139,1519,3588,18,4314,3619,3619,3619],[1063,2532,5547,3756,3756,700,1438,235,2531,1125,1125,1125,3588,3680,3588,3588,3588,3679,4771,1968,1968,1909,1473],[1063,3745,3745,4270,4270,4270,4270,4270,1125,1125,1519,2251,1319,2443,2443,1223,5281,2532,3588,3874,3588,3588,1124,2192,2192,2192,1680],[1161,3588,3588,2316,5281,5281,5281,2532,3874,1325,4771,5426,1722,240,240,2596,5547,2424],[2443,2443,3661,3661,3661,1722,1520,4750,1392,1392,1392,3588,2316,2532,3962,1473,1473,2962,2424,5547],[4355,240,240,1352,2532,2531,5547,4355,4771,1519,1519,1519,1519,1391,2316,2316],[1063,3004,3004,3004,3004,5547,1096,1096,1249,1249,4061,4061,4061,5228,5228,5228,2316,225,1519,950,3588,1860,1860,3588,3588,3962],[1161,1161,3588,1484,1392,1392,2316,5228,5228,1656,2531,1125,1125,1125,1223,1843,1843,1843,4771,1722,1484,1484,5567,5567,5567,5567,3588,4771,3686],[3825,3004,3004,2165,1484,1484,3326,846,2992],[2532,3825,134,3588,2962,3956,3588,1484,2532,1867,846,3956,3588,2992],[2532,3825,3825,2268,3004,3588,4491,2421,2421,1510,1510,3588,3588,450,450,757,757